Why Docker:
Before docker was invented, consider if we have to develope the app it has appserver in nodejs, postgresql db, mq and ansible orchetrisation.So need to find the os which is compatible for all the technology and its version, then for each component ie nodejs need to find the compatabile lib and dependenises(ext library) as well. Which is very difficult, then if replace the component from pogrgres to mongodb then same process which is time consuming and when new developer join he need to run lot of command to setup the env.Also if developer use different os and the same app is deployed in different test and prod env again the app will fail because of the compatability issue. So docker inveneted,on top of host os we can install docker, on top of docker we can create any number of container or instance.Our case its 4 container for 4 component, so each component has its own os, lib and dependencies we can export that to other envlike prod and test, so the compatability issue will be fixed.

Containers:
Container is the instance it will have its own process, network interface and mounts but it will share the host os kernal.On top of host os on top of docker we can can create any number of containers. 
What is Share host os kernal ?
Consider we have os like ubuntu, rhel, debian, sles all are different os but share the same os kernal which is linux.What differentiating each ie ubuntu, rhel, debian, sles is their softwares ie pkg, compiler, dev tool , ui etc which only differentiate the os but share same os kernal. So if the hardware os is any linux os on top we can create any number of docker container with different os , but cant create container with windows since its not share the same os kernal.
